# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Editor directories
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Secrets
secrets.*
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Dependencies (if any runtime code added later)
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Supervisor/Worker runtime artifacts
# .claude/   # [loomwright/setup-memory] disabled: a bare directory exclude defeats the negation below
# .supervisor/   # [loomwright/setup-memory] disabled: a bare directory exclude defeats the negation below
.worker-summary*.md

# `setup-memory.sh apply` ALWAYS writes a timestamped `.gitignore.backup.<ts>` sibling here
# (backup-first contract, setup-memory.sh:411-424) and a matching `.supervisor/config.json.backup.<ts>`.
# No pre-existing pattern matched them, so a routine `git add -A` would have staged them. The
# `.supervisor/` one is already covered by the managed block below; this line covers the root one.
.gitignore.backup.*

# Graphify local knowledge graph (large runtime state — Local Twin Step 3; never commit)
graphify-out/

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
publish/*
PRs and commits.json
temp/

# Junk artifact from a mis-invoked `learning-emit` (ledger path is POSITIONAL — omitting it
# writes the record to a file literally named after the flag). Third sighting; the durable fix
# is loomwright/scripts/test-no-junk-tracked-files.sh, this is the belt-and-braces backstop.
/--run-id
/--*
# >>> loomwright /setup memory BEGIN — committable Twin stores (managed block) >>>
# Negate CONTENTS, not the directory. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so the naive form
#     .claude/
#     !.claude/agent-memory/
# looks correct and silently does NOTHING. The `/*` form below excludes the directory's contents
# and leaves the directory itself traversable, so the `!` lines can re-include.
#
# Committed on purpose: the Twin's accumulated judgment (agent memory + distilled lessons),
# including their dot-prefixed provenance sidecars. Everything else under these two directories
# stays ignored — worktree checkouts, machine-local settings, session logs.
#
# Managed by `/setup memory`. Edit via that command (`/setup memory remove` reverts it);
# hand-edits inside these sentinels are overwritten on the next apply.
.claude/*
!.claude/agent-memory/
.supervisor/*
!.supervisor/memory/
# <<< loomwright /setup memory END <<<
